SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

SignPath artifact configuration for the Windows release. SignPath keeps its
own copy (project QtPass, default artifact configuration); this file is the
reviewed source of it, so change both together.

The Release installers workflow hands SignPath two bare files in turn
(upload-artifact archive: false): qtpass.exe, then the Inno Setup installer
built around the already signed qtpass.exe. The Qt libraries next to
qtpass.exe are never submitted; they are Qt's binaries, not ours to sign.
-->
<artifact-configuration xmlns="http://signpath.io/artifact-configuration/v1">
  <pe-file product-name="QtPass">
    <authenticode-sign />
  </pe-file>
</artifact-configuration>
